<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids mostly lower.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids mostly lower.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring and white wheat bids were mostly lower on Friday with some farm sales reported, several dealers said.</p>
<p>But the focus in the Pacific Northwest market would be the upcoming Pakistan tender for 450,000 tonnes Australian and/or U.S. wheat. CBOT March wheat was buoyed by optimisim for a large sale of U.S. wheat this weekend to Pakistan.</p>
<p>MGE spring wheat futures ended lower, with nearbys weaker on spreading and moderate commercial pressure.</p>
<p>MGE March wheat lost 2-3/4 cents to end at $3.84-3/4 a bushel.  </p>
